21:     """
22:     Fill the frame interior with two marker colors arranged in matching 2x2 diagonal quadrants.
23: 
24:     Input structure:
25:     - The dominant background contains one solid one-pixel-thick rectangular frame.
26:     - The frame has an even-height and even-width empty interior.
27:     - Exactly two one-pixel markers of different colors sit outside the frame.
28: 
29:     Rule:
30:     - A marker in the northwest or southeast side of the frame center supplies the
31:       main diagonal quadrants of the interior.
32:     - A marker in the northeast or southwest side supplies the other two quadrants.
33:     - Split the frame interior into row and column halves and fill each cell by
34:       the diagonal class of its half-position.
35: 
36:     Key insight:
37:     - The marker colors are not copied from their exact rows or columns; their
38:       coarse position relative to the frame center selects one of the two diagonal
39:       quadrant masks.
40:     """
